[%# The account menu's section for moving this browser to another web
    interface (App::Netdisco::Web::UI): a heading, then every interface by its
    short label, the one in use ticked and the others each a button that posts
    to /web_ui. Shared by every layout, so it lives with the classic views that
    every interface falls back to, and nothing here depends on how many
    interfaces there are. The same URL works in any interface, so the switch
    returns to the page it was pressed on, which the route reads from the
    Referer header rather than from a field here (see back_from_referer).
    With the classic interface alone there is nothing to choose and nothing is
    drawn. The section is bounded by dividers on both sides. -%]
[% IF web_uis.size > 1 %]
<li><hr class="dropdown-divider"></li>
<li><h6 class="dropdown-header">Interface</h6></li>
[% FOREACH ui IN web_uis %]
<li>
  [% IF ui.current %]
  <span class="dropdown-item-text fw-semibold" aria-current="true"><i class="fas fa-check fa-fw"></i> [% ui.short_label | html_entity %]</span>
  [% ELSE %]
  <form method="post" class="nd_inline-form nd_web-ui-switch" action="[% uri_for('/web_ui') | none %]">
    <input type="hidden" name="ui" value="[% ui.name | html_entity %]">
    <button type="submit" class="dropdown-item" title="[% ui.switch_title | html_entity %]"><i class="fas fa-fw"></i> [% ui.short_label | html_entity %]</button>
  </form>
  [% END %]
</li>
[% END %]
<li><hr class="dropdown-divider"></li>
[% END %]
